What is an Invariant?

An invariant is something that remains true after every iteration of the loop.

For this problem:

Invariant: After processing the first i elements, max stores the largest value seen so far.

This is the mindset interviewers want.

Golden Rule (Remember for Life)

Whenever you're finding a maximum or minimum, ask yourself:

What is my initial answer?
arr[0] if the array is guaranteed non-empty.
Integer.MIN_VALUE / Integer.MAX_VALUE if you plan to examine every element.
Have I already considered the first element?
If yes, start the loop at i = 1.
If no, start the loop at i = 0.

This simple rule will prevent one of the most common bugs in array problems.

